<article class="env-lemma" id="008D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/008D">Lemma <span data-tag="008D">6.21.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous map. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of sets on $X$. Then $f_*\mathcal{F}$ is a sheaf on $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This immediately follows from the fact that if $V = \bigcup V_ j$ is an open covering in $Y$, then $f^{-1}(V) = \bigcup f^{-1}(V_ j)$ is an open covering in $X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>